cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this codebook in your research, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
title: "EA 4FM Codebook for LLM-Assisted Qualitative Analysis"
abstract: >-
  A structured codebook for scoring participant testimony against Längle's
  Four Fundamental Motivations (4FM) framework, designed for use with Large
  Language Models as a research instrument. Built by multi-LLM cross-validation
  across three LLMs (Claude Sonnet 4.5, ChatGPT 5 Thinking, Gemini 2.5 Turbo)
  against four primary Längle sources (1992, 2002, 2003, 2011). Every code
  traces to a verbatim quote with citation. Companion to the WCET4 (2026) paper
  "Do You Understand?! Best Practices using Artificial Intelligence in
  Research (and Life)." Methodological predecessor to the EA 12FEP Codebook
  (https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20481464), which was built shortly after and
  refines and simplifies the build protocol of this 4FM codebook.
authors:
  - family-names: "Nelson-Zutter"
    given-names: "Graham"
    email: "graham@aestra.ca"
    affiliation: "MSc student, Existential Analysis & Logotherapy, University of Salzburg, Austria"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-9567-6512"
version: "1.0"
date-released: "2026-06-06"  # WCET4 presentation date (Sat 6 Jun 2026, Denver, CO)
license: "CC-BY-NC-ND-4.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/aestra-research/4fm-codebook"
url: "https://github.com/aestra-research/4fm-codebook"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.20483207"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.20483207"
    description: "Concept DOI (always resolves to the latest version)"
  - type: doi
